<title>SINGAPORE: U.S. elections to delay Iraq oil return - Subroto.</title>
<headline>U.S. elections to delay Iraq oil return - Subroto.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraqi oil will not return to world markets until after the U.S. elections in November, former OPEC secretary general Subroto said on Monday.</p>
<p>Speaking at the opening of the Asia-Pacific Petroleum Conference in Singapore, Subroto said the timing of the return of Iraqi oil to the markets was &quot;a difficult matter to predict being a political issue, but if it happens it will be after the U.S. elections in November.&quot;</p>
<p>Subroto, chairman of the Foundation of Indonesian Institute for Energy Economics, said that after last week's volatility in the oil markets, he expected crude prices to maintain current levels until the end of the year.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom +65 870 3080</p>
</text>
